ocation_regions": ["Europe", "Europe", "EMEA"]}, "experience_summary": "Venntro was a completely agile-based development environment, working in 2-week sprints with continuous deployment going on throughout. Venntro allowed me to develop my microservice based architecture skills, though I mainly worked on platform improvements, bringing new features to the 40 million members across 30,000 (white-label) sites that included adding features that replicated Tinder, with the caching of members in redis which allowed smooth operation, to working on our email and messaging platform micro-services. I was part of the team that moved the photo and asset storage from the bare-metal hosting provider’s storage to AWS S3 and AWS S3 Glacier. Venntro had a monolithic customer-facing website but had started to move towards Ruby-based microservice backends for payment processing, member data manipulation, caching and storage as well as messaging (emails and private messages). Show less", "is_current_experience": false, "is_startup_experience": false}], "type": "company-experiences"}, {"company_info": {"name": "Law Business Research", "domain": "lbresearch.com", "website": "http://www.lbresearch.com", "linkedin_url": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/law-business-research", "linkedin_slug": "law-business-research", "crunchbase_url": "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/law-business-research", "social_urls": ["https://twitter.com/wearelbr"], "phone_number": "'+44 20 7908 1181", "type": "company-info", "description": "Tech-enabled information services business powering the legal industry with intelligence, analytics and performance data", "industries": ["Information Technology"], "keywords": ["crossborder law & policy", "global news & insight", "rankings & benchmarking", "live events", "workflow tools", "data & analysis"], "technologies": ["Salesforce", "Cloudflare DNS", "Amazon SES", "Mailchimp Mandrill", "Mimecast", "Outlook", "Microsoft Office 365", "CloudFlare Hosting", "Message